'''''Euphorbia triangularis''''', commonly known as '''river naboom, river euphorbia''', '''chandelier-tree''' or '''tree euphorbia''', is a species of [[plant]] in the family [[Euphorbiaceae]] native to southern Africa.<ref>{{Cite web|url =http://pza.sanbi.org/euphorbia-triangularis |title = Euphorbia triangularis |website = Plantzafrica.com | publisher=South African National Biodiversity Institute |access-date = 1 January 2021 | first=Bathabile | last=Ndlovu| date =September 2018}}</ref>

